lson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-22T20:32:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the candidates and what are the priorities after TCU fired Sonny Dykes?","description":"Things started well for Dykes, but now the Horned Frogs are looking for a new coach and should have options.","published":"2026-11-22T19:55:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50323301/tcu-candidates-personnel-recruits","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman, Max Olson and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918136/quincy-rhodes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Quincy Rhodes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:15Z","intro":"Quincy Rhodes Jr. (born December 1, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Arkansas Razorbacks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Rhodes Jr. attended North Little Rock High School in North Little Rock, Arkansas. As a senior he had 84 tackles and 11.5 sacks. He was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl. Rhodes Jr. committed to the University of Arkansas to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Rhodes Jr. spent his first two years at Arkansas as a backup, appearing in 21 games with one start and recording 16 tackles and one sack. He became a full-time starter for the first time his junior year in 2025."}]}}